3. test_n2 | requirement: For n=2, length-2 segments are always good, so output must be 2. | technique: boundary value | oracle: ans != 2 | validity: n=2 inputs | value: n=2 handling.
4. test_all_zeros | requirement: All zeros satisfy condition for any triplet, so whole array is good, output=n. | technique: equivalence partition | oracle: ans != n | validity: inputs with all a_i=0 | value: trivial satisfaction.
5. test_all_ones | requirement: All ones fail condition for triplets, so longest good segment is 2 if n>=2 else 1. | technique: equivalence partition | oracle: ans not equal to expected (1 or 2) | validity: inputs with all a_i=1 | value: no triplet handling.
6. test_full_fibonacci | requirement: If entire array satisfies a_i = a_{i-1}+a_{i-2}, output must be n. | technique: decision rule | oracle: ans != n | validity: inputs where condition holds for all i>=3 | value: fully good array recognition.
